amneziawg-linux-kmod (1.0.20260927+awg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release of the patched fork (AmneziaWG 2.0 protocol), based on
    upstream 26f5df0. Changes in docs/CHANGELOG.md, among them:
  * AWG parameters are validated as a whole before anything is applied; a
    rejected "awg set" no longer leaves invalid values active (crashes of
    upstream #254 / #225) or a changed listen port.
  * Plain WireGuard, AWG 1.0 and AWG 2.0 peers without S3/S4 on one
    obfuscated interface, detected per peer and reported over netlink.
  * A replayed old handshake initiation can no longer switch a peer to
    unobfuscated framing.
  * I1-I5 size overflow, use-after-free on teardown, netlink dump with
    many peers and other upstream bugs fixed.
  * Builds on Linux 7.1/7.2, distro kernels with the new udp_tunnel API,
    RHEL/AlmaLinux 10.2-10.3; the zinc assembly files needed before 5.10
    are back.
  * Packaging: correct DKMS version in dkms.conf, debhelper compat 13.

 -- Advanced-WG <237044+V-Bantserov@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0300

